title: Developer Routes
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

This page documents the stable, developer-facing HTTP routes used by widgets, browser scripts, the PubConnector extension, and local automation.

Routes listed here are part of the intended integration surface. Internal helper routes and test-only routes are not part of the public contract and may change without notice.

!! Literature import and reading

; `POST /literatures`
: Import one or more BibTeX entries and create new `bibtex-entry` tiddlers.
: Request body: raw BibTeX text, or JSON with a `bibtex` field.
: Success response: JSON containing `status`, `code`, and created `tiddlers`.

; `GET /literatures/latest?days=60`
: Return recent literature items for widgets or dashboards.
: Query parameter: `days` is optional and defaults to the route's configured fallback.
: Success response: JSON containing `status`, `code`, and `items`.

; `POST /literature/upload-html`
: Upload a publisher HTML file and associate it with an existing literature tiddler by DOI.
: Request format: `multipart/form-data` with an uploaded file and a `url` field.
: Success response: JSON confirming the HTML file was processed and saved.

; `GET /literature/article/<title>`
: Open the cleaned article reader for a saved literature tiddler.
: Path parameter: URL-encoded tiddler title.
: Success response: HTML page for in-browser reading rather than JSON.

!! Metadata and lookup

; `POST /literature/find-doi`
: Find a DOI from article metadata.
: Request body: JSON with `title`, and optional `author` and `publisher` fields.
: Success response: JSON containing `status`, `code`, and DOI lookup `results`.

; `GET /literature/crossref/<doi>`
: Fetch Crossref work metadata for a DOI.
: Path parameter: URL-encoded DOI.
: Success response: JSON containing `status`, `code`, and Crossref `data`.

; `GET /literature/references/<doi>`
: Fetch reference data for a DOI-backed paper.
: Path parameter: URL-encoded DOI.
: Success response: JSON containing `status`, `code`, and reference `data`.

; `GET /literature/<doi>/cites`
: Fetch citation data for a DOI-backed paper.
: Path parameter: URL-encoded DOI.
: Success response: JSON containing `status`, `code`, citation `count`, and citation `data`.

!! Reading state and highlights

; `POST /literature/mark-read`
: Mark a DOI as read in the reading cache.
: Request body: JSON with a `doi` field.
: Success response: JSON containing `status`, `code`, and the stored DOI.

; `GET /literature/highlight/<title>`
: Read saved highlight data for a literature tiddler.
: Path parameter: URL-encoded tiddler title.
: Success response: JSON array of highlights. Returns an empty array when no highlights have been saved yet.

; `POST /literature/highlight/<title>`
: Save highlight data for a literature tiddler.
: Path parameter: URL-encoded tiddler title.
: Request body: JSON array of highlight objects.
: Success response: JSON containing `ok` and the saved highlight `count`.

; `POST /literature/highlight-render`
: Render a short TiddlyWiki wikitext note snippet to HTML for note previews.
: Request body: JSON with a `text` field.
: Success response: JSON containing rendered `html`.

!! Documentation conventions

* Document public routes here when they form part of the integration surface.
* Keep route module header comments as the source of truth for detailed request and response behavior.
* For each new public route, record the method, path, request shape, response shape, and one example request.